{
  "description": "CGM (2005) labor income process re-estimated from PSID; household labor income plus transfers, thousands of 1992 dollars (CPI-U); SRC male heads 20-65 (22-65 college); incomes under $2,000 (1992 $) dropped. Variances are in log points squared. Each set has one entry per education group and 'all', a single process for all households pooled over ages 20-65 (no education, cohort or other split).",
  "equation": "log Y = const + married*m + hhcomp*h + f(age) + v + e; v_t = v_{t-1} + u; Var(u)=s2_perm; Var(e)=s2_trans; retirement income = replacement_rate * exp(const + married*mean_married + hhcomp*mean_hhcomp + f(65))",
