  "replacement_rate_default": {
    "no_high_school": 0.87,
    "high_school": 0.78,
    "college": 0.68,
    "all": 0.69
  },
  "replacement_rate_default_note": "Richard's choice (2026-10-11): retired income incl. pensions over the profile at 65, CGM window 1969-1991, full sample (cgm/README.md). The pooled rate for all households (0.69) uses the same definition.",
  "ar1_alternative_note": "Optional replacement for the random walk, same profile: log Y = const + controls + f(age) + eta + iota; eta = s2_init draw at start_age, then eta_t = rho*eta_{t-1} + xi, Var(xi) = s2_innov; Var(iota) = s2_me (transitory shock plus measurement error). Specification of Choukhmane and de Silva (JF 2026); minimum distance on PSID autocovariances by age and lag (extend/scripts/ar1_process.py). For 'all', start_age 20 (college members start at 22).",
